{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 15, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Most Wondrous Itinerary for a Journey to the Fair Land of Japan**\n\n**Prologue**\nHark! Wherefore dost thou seek to tread upon the sacred soil of Nippon’s isle? If thy heart be set upon adventure and thy spirit craves the sights unseen then lend thine ear to this most cunning plan devised by mine own quill.\n\n**Act I: The Land of the Rising Sun’s First Embrace**\nUpon the morrow when first the sun doth kiss the earth set forth from Narita’s gate or Kansai’s hallowed halls. In Tokyo’s bustling streets where neon lights do dance and merchants hawk their wares let thou wander through Shibuya’s throngs and Shinjuku’s labyrinthine ways.\n\n**Act II: The Temples and Gardens of Tranquillity**\nThen to Kyoto’s ancient grace where temples stand in silent prayer and gardens paint the earth with hues most fair. Behold Kinkaku-ji’s golden splendor and Fushimi Inari’s vermilion gates. Let thy soul find peace in Arashiyama’s bamboo grove where whispers of the wind do sing.\n\n**Act III: The Spirit of the Samurai**\nTo Nara do go where deer do bow and gods in stone do gaze. Let thy heart be stirred by Todai-ji’s colossal Buddha and the tales of warriors bold. In Hiroshima let remembrance reign where peace doth bloom from sorrow’s pain.\n\n**Act IV: The Northern Wilderness and Hot Springs’ Embrace**\nTo Hokkaido’s frozen plains where winter’s breath is keen and Sapporo’s snowflakes dance. Or to Hakone’s steaming waters where weary bones find rest and Fuji’s peak doth watch o’er thee from afar.\n\n**Act V: The Culmination of Delights**\nLastly to Osaka’s kitchen where takoyaki and okonomiyaki do tempt the tongue. Let thy belly be filled with delights most wondrous and thy purse be lightened not.\n\n**Epilogue**\nThus ends thy journey through the land of Japan. May thy days be filled with joy and wonder and may thy heart forever hold the memories of this most fair voyage. Fare thee well and may fortune smile upon thy path!", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -1.5780527591705322}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.07835915684700012}, {"token": " Most", "logprob": -0.30257120728492737}, {"token": " W", "logprob": -0.19480778276920319}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -7.152531907195225e-06}, {"token": "rous", "logprob": -8.106198947643861e-06}, {"token": " It", "logprob": -0.25130367279052734}, {"token": "iner", "logprob": -0.0009460740839131176}, {"token": "ary", "logprob": -0.007307230960577726}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.07008983939886093}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.29305797815322876}, {"token": " Journey", "logprob": -0.5009442567825317}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.07890891283750534}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.1926978975534439}, {"token": " Fair", "logprob": -0.7306877970695496}, {"token": " Land", "logprob": -0.08496061712503433}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -2.038458114839159e-05}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.20363232493400574}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -0.10558713227510452}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -0.2880811393260956}, {"token": "P", "logprob": -3.16430926322937}, {"token": "rolog", "logprob": -0.0002383901592111215}, {"token": "ue", "logprob": -7.354942499659956e-05}, {"token": "**\n", "logprob": -0.46705466508865356}, {"token": "H", "logprob": -0.03156052902340889}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0003178806509822607}, {"token": "!", "logprob": -0.2196599245071411}, {"token": " Where", "logprob": -2.995572805404663}, {"token": "fore", "logprob": -0.0006039702566340566}, {"token": " dost", "logprob": -0.06938785314559937}, {"token": " thou", "logprob": -0.02094157785177231}, {"token": " seek", "logprob": -0.894344687461853}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.8747861385345459}, {"token": " tread", "logprob": -0.4578736126422882}, {"token": " upon", "logprob": -0.09148810058832169}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.01788453944027424}, {"token": " sacred", "logprob": -0.59701669216156